B.LE=s(["Liquid copper soaps","Neem oil sprays","Foliar sprays of beneficial microbe mixtures"],t.s)
B.Hj=new A.cx("Gray Leaf Spot","Cercospora zeae-maydis","Gray leaf spot is a persistent fungal disease characterized by rectangular, gray-to-brown spots on corn leaves. It overwinters in crop residues and can cause severe blighting under warm, moist conditions.",B.Od,B.P0,B.Mj,B.Mk,B.LE,"Approximately 3 to 4 weeks depending on severity.","Walk fields weekly after silking and check lower leaves for vein-bounded gray rectangular spots.",null)
B.MV=s(["Exserohilum turcicum fungus","Moderate temperatures (18-27\xb0C)","Prolonged moisture (heavy dew or rain)"],t.s)
B.OD=s(["Long, elliptical cigar-shaped grayish-green lesions","Dusty dark spores in centers of spots during humid spells","Premature leaf death"],t.s)
B.Lv=s(["Apply strobilurin or triazole fungicides","Rotate with non-grass crops","Plow crop residue down"],t.s)
B.Lo=s(["Choose resistant hybrids","Space plants properly","Destroy infected crop residues"],t.s)
B.LZ=s(["Copper hydroxide sprays","Neem oil formulations","Regular compost tea foliar sprays"],t.s)
B.Hf=new A.cx("Northern Leaf Blight","Exserohilum turcicum","Northern leaf blight produces large, cigar-shaped grayish-green lesions on corn leaves. It causes rapid tissue death under moderate, humid conditions and is highly damaging during the grain-fill stage.",B.MV,B.OD,B.Lv,B.Lo,B.LZ,"Approximately 3 to 5 weeks for foliage protection; existing spots do not heal.","Check lower leaves weekly during warm, moist weather. Catching cigar-shaped lesions early protects the ears.",null)
