B.Hd=new A.cx("Spider Mites (Two-spotted Spider Mite)","Tetranychus urticae","Two-spotted spider mites are tiny arachnids that suck cell sap from tomato leaves, causing yellow stippling and fine webbing. They thrive and multiply exponentially in hot, dry weather.",B.Ot,B.N9,B.NX,B.OF,B.Nt,"Approximately 2 to 3 weeks if mite population is suppressed early.","Inspect leaf undersides weekly for tiny moving dots during hot, dry spells. A magnifying glass helps detect early webbing.",null)
